{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherNotation\/number"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlothernotation\/number"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"number","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLOtherNotationV6numberAA14MXLNumberLevelVvp","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherNotation"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"number"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOtherNotation":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The other-notation type is used to define any notations not yet in the MusicXML format. It handles notations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where more specific extension elements such as other-dynamics and other-technical are not appropriate. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute can be used to specify a particular notation, allowing application interoperability without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requiring every SMuFL glyph to have a MusicXML element equivalent. Using the other-notation type without the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute allows for extended representation, though without application interoperability."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlothernotation","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOtherNotation","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLOtherNotation","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLOtherNotation","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherNotation","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"title":"MXLNumberLevel","abstract":[{"text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOtherNotation/number":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherNotation\/number","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"number","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlothernotation\/number","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"}}}